mirco-blis holds C sources of three projects, each under its own licence.
They were downloaded on 2026-10-27 from the official upstreams named here.

BLIS 2.1
  From:     https://github.com/flame/blis/archive/refs/tags/2.1.tar.gz
  SHA-256:  901752ec596cd63421ea45a6a06a9f34491cf5ae01cea412ece05f97a2690a96
  Licence:  BSD 3-Clause, c/blis/LICENSE
  Kept:     LICENSE CREDITS README.md CHANGELOG Makefile common.mk configure
            config_registry blis.pc.in build config frame kernels
            ref_kernels addon sandbox, unchanged.
  Left out: blastest (the f2c translation of the BLAS tests), testsuite,
            test, docs, examples, ci, vendor, RELEASING.md, CONTRIBUTING.md,
            INSTALL.

LAPACK, the C translation of lapack-netlib in OpenBLAS 0.3.34
  From:     https://github.com/OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS/releases/download/v0.3.34/OpenBLAS-0.3.34.tar.gz
  SHA-256:  cd7e129868320cc2d033afa920e31202dfe0b8066a5b66661900ccc0f197dfed
  Licence:  the modified BSD licence of LAPACK, c/lapack/LICENSE
            (lapack-netlib/LICENSE); OpenBLAS's own BSD 3-Clause licence,
            c/lapack/LICENSE.OpenBLAS.
  Kept:     the 126 C files listed in c/lapack/FILES.txt, unchanged: the
            routines dgesv, dgetrf, dgetrs, dgeqrf, dorgqr, dormqr, dpotrf,
            dpotrs, dgesdd, dsyevd, dgeev and dgelsd, and every routine they
            call, found by linking them against BLIS until no symbol was left.

pocketfft, from NumPy 1.26.4
  From:     https://github.com/numpy/numpy/releases/download/v1.26.4/numpy-1.26.4.tar.gz
            (numpy/fft/_pocketfft.c)
  SHA-256:  2a02aba9ed12e4ac4eb3ea9421c420301a0c6460d9830d74a9df87efa4912010
  Licence:  BSD 3-Clause, the licence of NumPy, c/pocketfft/LICENSE.numpy;
            copyright of the code 2004-2018 Max-Planck-Society, Martin Reinecke.
  Kept:     c/pocketfft/_pocketfft.c.orig, the file as NumPy ships it.
  Changed:  c/pocketfft/pocketfft.c is made from it by tools/make-pocketfft.pl:
            the includes of Python and NumPy and the functions over PyObject
